"""
Decision tree training — Bhardwaj et al. CCS 2024
"Securely Training Decision Trees Efficiently" (ePrint 2024/1077)
Microsoft Research India — implemented in MP-SPDZ PR #1449
(fork: https://github.com/sandy9999/MP-SPDZ, branch master, commit 87d1e5c)

Communication complexity O(mN log N + hmN + hN log N),
improvement of ~min(h, m, log N) over Hamada et al.

The algorithmic improvement is in the fork's Compiler/decision_tree.py, whose
TreeTrainer has a different interface than upstream MP-SPDZ:
TreeTrainer(x, y, h, binary=False, attr_lengths=None, n_threads=None).train(),
with x attribute-major (m rows of n values) and BINARY labels y (multi-class
labels are not supported by the fork; n_classes is ignored here).
Use with /opt/mp-spdz-bhardwaj instead of /opt/mp-spdz.
The FHE-PPML reproduction (scripts/run_baselines.sh) uses the fork's own
Programs/Source/bench-dt.mpc instead.

Compile (from /opt/mp-spdz-bhardwaj):
  ./compile.py -R 64 dt_train_bhardwaj <n_train> <m> <n_levels> <n_classes> [n_threads]

Run:
  Scripts/ring.sh dt_train_bhardwaj <n_train> <m> <n_levels> <n_classes> [n_threads]
"""

from Compiler.decision_tree import TreeTrainer

n_train   = int(program.args[1])
m         = int(program.args[2])
n_levels  = int(program.args[3])
n_classes = int(program.args[4])
n_threads = int(program.args[5]) if len(program.args) > 5 else 1

print_ln("=== Decision Tree (Bhardwaj et al. CCS 2024) ===")
print_ln("n_train=%s  m=%s  depth=%s  classes=%s  threads=%s",
         n_train, m, n_levels, n_classes, n_threads)

X = sint.Matrix(m, n_train)          # attribute-major, as the fork's TreeTrainer expects
y = sint.Array(n_train)

@for_range_opt(n_train)
def _(i):
    row = sint.get_input_from(0, size=m)
    for j in range(m):
        X[j][i] = row[j]
    y[i] = sint.get_input_from(0)

trainer = TreeTrainer(X, y, n_levels, n_threads=n_threads)
trainer.train()

print_ln("=== Training complete ===")
